# Defect 382, 2026-10-06. An index past the end of a constant laid out as a
# static block aborts at the read, as it did when the read built the array:
# `hero_array_at` asks the block's length, which the static header carries
# (panel 195's R1). The line before the abort prints; under `--sanitize` the
# constant is built at every read (R2) and aborts the same way.

constant K: [i64]
    [1, 2, 3]

function at(i: i64) -> i64
    return K[i]

function main()
    print(at(i: 2))
    print(at(i: 3))
